Article 3 (Use) The national emblem may be used on the following documents, facilities, or goods:
1. Official documents sent to foreign countries, international organizations, or foreign agencies in the Republic of Korea;
2. Letters of appointment of public officials of Grade I or an equivalent higher grade (including public officials belonging to the Senior Civil Service);
3. Orders and certificates of decorations and presidential commendation certificates;
4. Identification cards of national public officials;
5. Diplomas and degree certificates of national or public universities;
6. Buildings of diplomatic missions abroad;
7. Government-owned ships and aircraft;
8. Currency;
9. Other documents, facilities, or goods for which the head of a central administrative agency deems the national emblem necessary.
